# PROGRESS.md's session log has one shared insertion point (right after
# **Last updated:**, at the top) that every session writes to. The `union`
# merge driver is git's built-in strategy for append-style logs: on a
# same-spot collision it keeps both sides' lines instead of raising a
# conflict. See CLAUDE.md section 7 point 6 for the full policy this backs up
# (the ledger entry's own fresh, short-lived branch is the primary fix; this
# is the backstop for a genuine same-instant collision or a hand-edit).
PROGRESS.md merge=union
